#import "templates/resolution.typ": *

#show: resolution.with(
  number: 2,
  subtitle: [Adopting Amended and Restated Bylaws],
  short-title: [Board Consent Adopting Amended and Restated Bylaws],
  kind: "written-consent",
  date: blank[October \_\_, 2026],
  directors: ("Aadish Verma", "Ashwin Naren", "Vinayak Vikram", "Weston Yoo"),
  draft: true,
  exhibits: (
    exhibit("A", [Amended and Restated Bylaws of Project Pixel Orbital])[
      #align(center)[
        _a California nonprofit public benefit corporation_
        #v(1em)
        (attached)
      ]
    ],
  ),
)

#whereas[the sole incorporator of the Corporation, by written action taken
pursuant to Section 5134 of the California Corporations Code effective
September 30, 2026 (the "Incorporator Action"), adopted bylaws of the
Corporation (the "Original Bylaws") and elected the undersigned as the initial
directors of the Corporation;]

#whereas[the Board, by Unanimous Written Consent in Lieu of Organizational
Meeting effective September 30, 2026 ("Resolution No. 1"), fixed the authorized
number of directors, elected the officers of the Corporation, and took certain
other organizational actions;]

#whereas[Article 15 of the Original Bylaws and Section 5150(a) of the
California Corporations Code authorize the Board to adopt, amend, or repeal
bylaws;]

#whereas[the Board wishes to amend and restate the Original Bylaws in their
entirety, among other things to revise the qualifications of Directors, to
provide for one-year terms of Directors, and to revise the offices of the
Corporation, and to remove any doubt regarding the execution and
certification of the Original Bylaws; and]

#whereas[the Board has determined that the adoption of the Amended and Restated
Bylaws of the Corporation in the form attached hereto as Exhibit A (the
"Restated Bylaws") is advisable and in the best interests of the Corporation
and its charitable purposes;]

#now-therefore()

#article[Adoption of Amended and Restated Bylaws]

#resolved[that, pursuant to Article 15 of the Original Bylaws and Section
5150(a) of the California Corporations Code, the Restated Bylaws are hereby
approved and adopted as the Bylaws of the Corporation, amending, restating, and
superseding the Original Bylaws in their entirety, effective as of the
effective date of this Consent;]

#resolved[that, to the extent the Original Bylaws were for any reason not
validly adopted, executed, or certified, the Board hereby adopts the Restated
Bylaws as the Bylaws of the Corporation pursuant to Section 5150(a) of the
California Corporations Code, with the same effect;]

#resolved[that the resolutions set forth in Sections 2 through 7 of this
Consent are adopted under, and shall take effect immediately after the
adoption of, the Restated Bylaws; and]

#resolved[that the Secretary of the Corporation elected below is hereby
directed to complete and execute the Certificate of Secretary appended to the
Restated Bylaws, to keep the original or a copy of the Restated Bylaws at the
principal office of the Corporation in accordance with Sections 9.6.4.1 and
12.3 of the Restated Bylaws, and to insert the Restated Bylaws and this Consent
in the minute book of the Corporation.]

#article[Directors]

#resolved[that, pursuant to Section 7.1.1 of the Restated Bylaws, the exact
authorized number of Directors of the Corporation remains fixed at four (4),
until changed by further resolution of the Board;]

#resolved[that, pursuant to Section 7.3 of the Restated Bylaws, each of the
following persons is hereby elected as a Director of the Corporation for a
term of one (1) year, and until the election and qualification of such
Director's successor, or until such Director's earlier resignation or removal
in accordance with the Restated Bylaws and the California Nonprofit Corporation
Law:]

#names[Aadish Verma][Ashwin Naren][Vinayak Vikram][Weston Yoo]

#resolved[that the term of office of each such person as a Director under the
Incorporator Action shall end upon such person's election hereunder, each such
person, by executing this Consent, consents to such election, and the Board
finds that no Director's term is thereby extended beyond that for which such
Director was elected, as required by Article 15(b) of the Original Bylaws; and]

#resolved[that the Board finds that each of the foregoing Directors either is
a student at Stanford Online High School or is over the age of eighteen (18),
as required by Section 7.1.2 of the Restated Bylaws, and that at least two (2)
of the foregoing Directors reside in the State of California, as required by
Section 7.1.3 of the Restated Bylaws.]

#article[Officers]

#resolved[that all persons elected or appointed as officers of the Corporation
under Sections 2, 3, and 4 of Resolution No. 1, namely Weston Yoo as
Chairperson of the Board, Ashwin Naren as President, Vinayak Vikram as
Secretary, Aadish Verma as Treasurer and Chief Financial Officer, Aadish Verma
as Station Control Operator, and Michelle Yoo as Government Affairs Officer,
are hereby removed from such offices pursuant to Section 9.3
of the Restated Bylaws, effective immediately prior to the elections below,
without prejudice to any action taken by any of them in such capacity before
such removal;]

#resolved[that the office of Station Control Operator, which is not provided
for in the Restated Bylaws, and the office of Government Affairs Officer
designated under Section 4 of Resolution No. 1 are hereby abolished, together
with all duties, powers, and authority conferred on either office, including
the authority of the Government Affairs Officer to execute IRS Form 2848 on
behalf of the Corporation;]

#resolved[that, pursuant to Sections 9.1 and 9.2 of the Restated Bylaws, the
following persons are hereby elected to the offices set forth opposite their
names, each to serve for a term of one (1) year and at the discretion of the
Board until such officer's successor is elected, or until such officer's
earlier resignation or removal:]

#block(breakable: false, pad(left: 2em, table(
  columns: (1fr, 1fr),
  stroke: none,
  inset: (x: 0pt, y: 4pt),
  table.header([*Name*], [*Office*]),
  [Ashwin Naren], [Chairperson of the Board & President (chief executive)],
  [Aadish Verma], [Vice President],
  [Weston Yoo], [Secretary],
  [Vinayak Vikram], [Treasurer and Chief Financial Officer]
)))

#resolved[that, the Board having designated both a Chairperson and a
President, the Board hereby establishes the specific duties of each position
as required by Section 9.6.1 of the Restated Bylaws, as follows: (a) the
Chairperson shall preside at, or select the Director who shall preside at,
each meeting of the Board as provided in Sections 7.13 and 9.6.1 of the
Restated Bylaws, shall lead the Board in carrying out its governance and
oversight responsibilities, and shall perform such other duties as the Board
may assign; and (b) the President, there being no other person designated as
chief executive, shall be the chief executive of the Corporation with the
powers and duties set forth in Sections 9.6.2 and 9.7 of the Restated Bylaws,
and shall supervise, direct, and control the Corporation's day-to-day
activities, business, and affairs, subject to the control of the Board;]

#resolved[that the Board notes that the Chairperson is a Director, as required
by Section 9.6.1 of the Restated Bylaws; and]

#resolved[that the Board notes that neither the Secretary nor the Treasurer
serves concurrently as the President or the Chairperson, and that the Vice
President, who
performs the duties of the President in the President's absence or disability
pursuant to Section 9.6.3 of the Restated Bylaws, holds neither the office of
Secretary nor that of Treasurer, as required by Section 9.1 of the Restated
Bylaws.]

#article[Effect on Resolution No. 1]

#resolved[that Sections 2 (Election of Officers), 3 (Station Control
Operator), and 4 (Creation of Office of Government Affairs Officer; Election of
Michelle Yoo) of Resolution No. 1 are hereby superseded in their entirety by
Section 3 of this Consent, prospectively from the effective date of this
Consent;]

#resolved[that, except as provided in this Section 4, Resolution No. 1,
including the Conflict of Interest Policy adopted thereby, remains in full
force and effect;]

#resolved[that each reference in Section 7 (Deposit Account) of Resolution No.
1 to the Government Affairs Officer shall be construed as a reference to the
President, such that the authority conferred by that Section shall be
exercised by the Treasurer and the President, acting jointly;]

#resolved[that each reference in Resolution No. 1 or in the Conflict of
Interest Policy to a provision of the "Bylaws" shall be construed as a
reference to the corresponding provision of the Restated Bylaws; and]

#resolved[that each reference in Resolution No. 1 to the Chairperson, the
President, the Secretary, or the Treasurer shall be construed as a reference
to the person holding such office from time to time.]

#article[Ratification of Prior Actions]

#resolved[that the Incorporator Action, the adoption of the Original Bylaws,
the election of the initial Directors, Resolution No. 1, and all other actions
heretofore taken by the incorporator, the Directors, and the officers of the
Corporation in the name and on behalf of the Corporation, to the extent
consistent with the purposes and intent of the foregoing resolutions, are
hereby ratified, confirmed, and approved in all respects as acts of the
Corporation, notwithstanding any defect in the adoption, execution, or
certification of the Original Bylaws.]

#article[Government Filings]

#resolved[that the officers of the Corporation are hereby authorized and
directed, in the name and on behalf of the Corporation, to prepare, execute,
and file with the California Secretary of State a Statement of Information
(Form SI-100) reflecting the officers elected by this Consent, whether as the
initial Statement of Information required by Section 6210 of the California
Corporations Code or as an updated statement, and to pay all related fees;
and]

#resolved[that the officers of the Corporation are hereby authorized and
directed to report the adoption of the Restated Bylaws on the Corporation's
next annual information return filed with the Internal Revenue Service, and on
any other return or report on which such change is required to be reported.]

#article[General Authority]

#resolved[that the officers of the Corporation are, and each of them is,
hereby authorized and directed, in the name and on behalf of the Corporation,
to take all such further actions, to execute and deliver all such further
agreements, instruments, certificates, and documents, to make all such
filings, and to pay all such fees and expenses, as they or any of them may deem
necessary or appropriate to carry out the intent and accomplish the purposes of
the foregoing resolutions.]
